.TH DOCKERO 1 "July 2026" "v1.0.0" "Dockero Manual"
.SH NAME
dockero \- Lightweight Bash-based CLI enhancement layer for Docker and Podman
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dockero
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.br
.B dockero
.I command
[\fIarguments...\fR] [\fIflags...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dockero
is a wrapper and enhancement suite designed to make Docker and Podman workflows more accessible, readable, and maintainable. It adds colorized output, structured logging, automatic Nvidia GPU configuration, unified runtime compatibility (Docker/Podman), an interactive learning interface, system diagnostic/healing tools, and plugin extensibility.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the global help manual or subcommand-specific help when preceded by a command.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and active runtime configuration.

.SH COMMAND CATEGORIES
The following subcommands are supported, grouped by functional categories:

.SS 1. Container Management
.TP
.BI create " container_name" " image"
Create and start a new container. Validates that the container name conforms to Docker specifications.
.TP
.BI start " container_name"
Start a stopped container.
.TP
.BI stop " container_name"
Stop a running container.
.TP
.BI remove " container_name"
Remove a container.
.TP
.BI rename " old_name" " new_name"
Rename an existing container.
.TP
.BI list " [img]"
List running containers. Add \fBimg\fR as an argument to list local images instead.

.SS 2. Image Management
.TP
.BI export " container_name" " output_file.tar"
Export a container's filesystem to a tar archive.
.TP
.BI import " input_file.tar" " image_name"
Import a tar archive filesystem as a new Docker image.
.TP
.BI registry " [login|push|pull|list|search|logout]"
Manage private registry authentications and operations.

.SS 3. Volumes & Networking
.TP
.BI volume " [list|create|remove|inspect|attach|prune]"
Perform volume operations with cleaner formatting.
.TP
.BI net " [new|delete|add|connect|disconnect|rename|prune|list|inspect]"
Manage Docker/Podman networks.

.SS 4. Multi-Container Projects
.TP
.BI setup " [project_name]"
Create standardized workspace templates for applications (e.g. Nginx, PostgreSQL).
.TP
.BI compose " [up|down|start|stop|restart|ps|logs]"
Wrapper for docker-compose operations.
.TP
.BI env " [list|use|show|create|delete|switch]"
Manage environment-specific configuration files (.env).
.TP
.B validate
Check project files, Dockerfiles, and compose configurations for syntax correctness.

.SS 5. Synchronization & Backup
.TP
.BI sync " [push|pull|watch|status|init]"
Synchronize directories and data into/from running containers.

.SS 6. Monitoring & Health
.TP
.BI monitor " [top|stats|health|logs|watch]"
View container performance metrics, process trees, check health in batch, or watch output.
.TP
.B dashboard
Start a terminal-based live monitoring dashboard.
.TP
.BI heal " [check|fix|auto|diagnose|cleanup|monitor]"
Diagnose container/network issues and automatically apply remediation steps.

.SS 7. Security & Secrets
.TP
.BI secrets " [create|ls|rm|show|inspect]"
Manage credentials, keys, and confidential environment parameters.

.SS 8. System & Utilities
.TP
.BI system " [service|config|info|cleanup|install|dev]"
Configure global system integrations, clean up unused caches, view system specs, or set up development symbolic links.
.TP
.BI plugin " [list|install|remove]"
Manage custom subcommand plugins.

.SS 9. Interactive Learning
.TP
.BI learn " [start|basic|intermediate|advanced|docker|concepts|examples]"
Launch interactive guided lessons covering Docker concepts and practices.
.TP
.BI explain " subcommand"
Fetch internal instruction manuals for any subcommand.
.TP
.B wizard
Start a conversational CLI setup configuration helper.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Dockero reads configuration variables from
.B ~/.dockero/config
if it exists. This file is sourced as a shell script.

.SS Supported Config Variables:
.TP
.B DOCKERO_RUNTIME
Configures the underlying virtualization runtime. Set to \fBdocker\fR (default) or \fBpodman\fR.
.TP
.B DOCKERO_RESTART_POLICY
Defines default restart parameters for created containers. Defaults to \fBunless-stopped\fR.
.TP
.B DOCKERO_DEFAULT_PORT
Port mapped to host for quick containers. Defaults to \fB80\fR.
.TP
.B DOCKERO_LOG_TIMESTAMPS
Boolean (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR). If set, prepends timestamps to log messages.
.TP
.B DOCKERO_AUTO_GPU_ENABLED
Boolean (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR). Automatically configures Nvidia container runtime parameters if a compatible GPU is detected.

.SH EXTENSIBILITY (PLUGINS)
Users can extend the CLI with custom scripts placed in the
.B ~/.dockero/commands/
directory.
.PP
Plugins can be managed using the built-in
.B dockero plugin
subcommand:
.TP
.BI "dockero plugin install " "name" " url"
Downloads and installs a custom script from a raw script URL.
.TP
.BI "dockero plugin list"
Lists all active custom commands and their helper descriptions.
.TP
.BI "dockero plugin remove " "name"
Uninstalls the specified plugin.
.PP
If a script named
.B ~/.dockero/commands/backup.sh
exists, calling \fBdockero backup\fR will automatically source it and run its \fBbackup\fR function.
The plugin script should define two functions:
.IP 1.
.BI <command_name>_help()
displays help instructions when running \fBdockero explain <command_name>\fR.
.IP 2.
.BI <command_name>()
contains the execution logic. Sourced parameters are accessible via the \fBargs\fR array.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/dockero
Symlink to the main runner script.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/dockero/
Root folder containing Dockero's bin, lib, documentation, and completion assets.
.TP
.I ~/.dockero/config
User configuration overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.dockero/commands/
Custom plugin scripts.
.SH COMPILATION & BUILD
Dockero utilizes a compilation-focused layout where individual subcommands and utilities are bundled into a single standalone executable.
.PP
To compile Dockero from source, execute:
.B make build
.PP
To run the full test suite and shell validations, execute:
.B make test
.PP
To clean and bundle a production release, run:
.B make dist

